/-!
# `𝓘 ^ n M` is quasi-coherent, and its two spellings agree

Let `F` be an algebraic space, `𝓘 ⊆ 𝒪_F` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `M` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-module.  This file computes the sections of the submodule `𝓘 ^ n M` over an
affine étale chart `U`: they are exactly `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`, with no sheafification left over.
Two things follow, neither of which was available before.

* `𝓘 ^ n M` is quasi-coherent, hence — on a locally Noetherian space and for coherent `M` —
  coherent, and so is the quotient `M / 𝓘 ^ n M`.
* The two unrelated spellings of `𝓘 ^ n M` in this repository agree.  One is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule`, the local-membership closure of the chartwise
  products, in which the Artin–Rees development of Stacks 07UL is stated; the other is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple`, the least sheaf submodule dominating those
  products, in which the category `Coh(F, 𝓘)` of coherent `𝓘`-adic systems is defined.  The
  comparison needs no hypothesis at all and is the bridge between the two developments.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image` — the chartwise
  computation everything here rests on: along a chart morphism over which both `M` and `𝓘` do
  base change, `𝓘(V) ^ n · M(V)` is generated by the restrictions of `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine` — the sections of
  `𝓘 ^ n M` over an affine chart are `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowSubmodule` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowSubmodule` — `𝓘 ^ n M` is cartesian on
  affine charts, hence quasi-coherent.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSubmodule` — **the two spellings of
  `𝓘 ^ n M` agree**, unconditionally.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherent_idealPowerMultiple` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoherent_idealPowerQuotient` — on a locally Noetherian space,
  `𝓘 ^ n M` and `M / 𝓘 ^ n M` are coherent for coherent `M`.

## Implementation notes

The affine sections are computed by faithfully flat descent along a finite affine étale covering
family, in the form `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict`.  The descent is
applied to the *chartwise* submodule `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`, not to a sheaf submodule, which is why
the covering sieve has to be produced in two steps: a section of `𝓘 ^ n M` restricts into the
chartwise product of `𝓘 ^ n` with `M` along a covering sieve
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sieve_of_mem_idealPowSmul`), and a section of *that* restricts
into the product of the honest `n`-th power of the ideal of sections along a further one
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sieve_mem_pow_chartIdeal_smul_top`), the powers of a sheaf of
ideals being themselves a closure.

Cartesianity of `𝓘 ^ n M` on affine charts splits as usual.  Injectivity of the base change
comparison is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.injective_sectionsBaseChange_of_injective_app` applied to
the inclusion into `M`, which needs only flatness of the restriction map between affine charts.
Surjectivity is the chartwise computation above, transported across the inclusion; this is the
step the implementation note of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_submodule_unit_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`
records as unavailable for a general submodule — it is available here because the sections of
this particular submodule are known.

The comparison of the two spellings needs no hypothesis because both are characterized by the
same chartwise universal property: `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_le_iff` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule_le_iff` test a sheaf submodule against the same
chartwise condition, so the two least elements coincide.  The scheme-level counterpart,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerComparison.idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSmul`, does need
quasi-coherence, because there the second model is *defined* by its affine sections.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07UL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07UL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07UD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07UD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry

universe u m

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)

/-! ### The chartwise product is generated by the restrictions of the chartwise product above -/

/-- The sections of a module over a chart are generated by the restrictions of its sections over
a larger chart, as soon as the base change comparison along that chart morphism is surjective.

This is the `⊤` case of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.span_image_chartRestrictLinear_eq`, which it
cannot be read off from: that lemma is stated for a sheaf submodule, and `⊤` is not the module
itself but a submodule isomorphic to it. -/
theorem span_range_chartRestrictLinear_eq_top (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF)
    {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : V ⟶ U)
    (hM : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange M φ)) :
    Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (Set.range fun x : M.val.obj (op U) => chartRestrictLinear M φ x) = ⊤ :=
  (chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top M φ).1 hM

/-- **The chartwise computation.**  Along a morphism `φ : V ⟶ U` of étale charts over which the
sections of `M` and the sections of `𝓘` are both base changes, the chartwise product
`𝓘(V) ^ n · M(V)` is generated by the restrictions of `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`.

The ideal of sections over `V` is the extension of the ideal of sections over `U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ideal_map_chartRestrict_chartIdeal`), so a section of `𝓘(V) ^ n` is a
combination of restrictions of sections of `𝓘(U) ^ n`; the sections of `M` over `V` are in turn
generated by restrictions of sections over `U`, and restriction is multiplicative on the two
factors. -/
theorem pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image (I : IdealSheaves B S hS F hF)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (n : ℕ) {U V : SmallEtale B S hS F} (φ : V ⟶ U)
    (hM : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange M φ))
    (hI : Function.Surjective (sectionsBaseChange I.toSheafOfModules φ)) :
    chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I V ^ n •
        (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (M.val.obj (op V)))
      ≤ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (chartRestrictLinear M φ '' ↑(chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I U ^ n •
          (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (M.val.obj (op U))))) := by
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) φ
  set P : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (M.val.obj (op U)) :=
    chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I U ^ n • ⊤ with hP
  set Q : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (M.val.obj (op V)) :=
    Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
      (chartRestrictLinear M φ '' (P : Set (M.val.obj (op U)))) with hQ
  -- restrictions of sections of `𝓘(U) ^ n` carry every restricted section of `M` into `Q`,
  -- hence so does the whole extended ideal
  have hmapT : Ideal.map (algebraMap (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V))
      (chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I U ^ n) ≤
        Q.colon (Set.range fun x : M.val.obj (op U) => chartRestrictLinear M φ x) :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun a ha => Submodule.mem_colon.2 <| by
      rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
      change chartRestrict (hF := hF) φ a • chartRestrictLinear M φ x ∈ Q
      rw [← chartRestrictLinear_smul M φ a x]
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨a • x, Submodule.smul_mem_smul ha Submodule.mem_top, rfl⟩
  have hVpow : chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I V ^ n =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (chartRing B S hS F hF V))
        (chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I U ^ n) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, ideal_map_chartRestrict_chartIdeal B S hS F hF I φ hI]
  refine Submodule.smul_le.2 fun r hr y _ => ?_
  have hr' := hmapT (hVpow.le hr)
  rw [← Submodule.colon_span, span_range_chartRestrictLinear_eq_top B S hS F hF M φ hM] at hr'
  exact Submodule.mem_colon.1 hr' y Submodule.mem_top

/-! ### The sections of `𝓘 ^ n M` over an affine chart -/

/-- A section of `𝓘 ^ n M` over a chart restricts, along a covering sieve, into the chartwise
product of the honest `n`-th power of the ideal of sections with the sections of `M`.

Both of the two closures involved are unwound: the product with a sheaf of ideals, and the power
of that sheaf of ideals. -/
theorem exists_sieve_mem_pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_of_mem_idealPowSubmodule
    (I : IdealSheaves B S hS F hF) (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (n : ℕ)
    {U : SmallEtale B S hS F} {t : M.val.obj (op U)}
    (ht : t ∈ chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowSubmodule I n M) U) :
    ∃ Sv : Sieve U, Sv ∈ SmallEtale.topology B S hS F U ∧
      ∀ ⦃Y : SmallEtale B S hS F⦄ (g : Y ⟶ U), Sv g →
        chartRestrictLinear M g t ∈ chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I Y ^ n •
          (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF Y) (M.val.obj (op Y))) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨S₀, hS₀, hS₀'⟩ :=
    exists_sieve_of_mem_idealPowSmul B S hS F hF I n (⊤ : M.Submodule) ht
  let T : Sieve U :=
    { arrows := fun Y g => chartRestrictLinear M g t ∈
        chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I Y ^ n •
          (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF Y) (M.val.obj (op Y)))
      downward_closed := by
        intro Y Y' g hg k
        rw [chartRestrictLinear_comp M g k t]
        exact map_mem_pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top B S hS F hF I M k n hg }
  refine ⟨T, ?_, fun Y g hg => hg⟩
  refine (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F).transitive hS₀ T ?_
  intro Y g hg
  obtain ⟨S₁, hS₁, hS₁'⟩ :=
    exists_sieve_mem_pow_chartIdeal_smul_top B S hS F hF I M n _ (hS₀' g hg)
  refine (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F).superset_covering ?_ hS₁
  intro Y' k hk
  change chartRestrictLinear M (k ≫ g) t ∈ _
  rw [chartRestrictLinear_comp M g k t]
  exact hS₁' k hk

/-- **The sections of `𝓘 ^ n M` over an affine étale chart are `𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)`.**

One inclusion is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_chartSubmodule` and
holds over every chart.  The other is faithfully flat descent: the section restricts into the
chartwise product over a covering sieve, over every affine member of that sieve the chartwise
product is generated by the restrictions of the chartwise product over `U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image`), and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict` descends that to `U`. -/
theorem chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine (I : IdealSheaves B S hS F hF)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M)
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts I.toSheafOfModules) (n : ℕ)
    {U : SmallEtale B S hS F} (hU : IsAffine (chartScheme U)) :
    chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowSubmodule I n M) U
      = chartSectionIdeal B S hS F hF I U ^ n •
        (⊤ : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF U) (M.val.obj (op U))) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun t ht => ?_)
    (pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_chartSubmodule B S hS F hF I n U)
  obtain ⟨Sv, hSv, hSv'⟩ :=
    exists_sieve_mem_pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_of_mem_idealPowSubmodule
      B S hS F hF I M n ht
  refine mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict B S hS F hF hMcart hU _ t hSv fun w ρ hw hρ => ?_
  exact pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image B S hS F hF I M n ρ
    (hMcart U w hU hw ρ).2 (hIcart U w hU hw ρ).2 (hSv' ρ hρ)

/-! ### `𝓘 ^ n M` is cartesian on affine charts, hence quasi-coherent -/

/-- **`𝓘 ^ n M` is cartesian on affine charts** when `M` and `𝓘` are.

Injectivity of the base change comparison uses only the inclusion `𝓘 ^ n M ⟶ M` and flatness of
the restriction map between affine charts.  Surjectivity is the computation of the affine
sections, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine`, together
with the chartwise generation statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image`. -/
theorem isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowSubmodule (I : IdealSheaves B S hS F hF)
    (M : Modules.{u, m} B S hS F hF) (hMcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts M)
    (hIcart : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts I.toSheafOfModules) (n : ℕ) :
    IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (idealPowModule I n M) := by
  intro U V hU hV φ
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) φ
  refine ⟨injective_sectionsBaseChange_of_injective_app (idealPowModuleι I n M) φ
      (flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine φ hU hV) (fun x y hxy => Subtype.ext hxy)
      (hMcart U V hU hV φ), ?_⟩
  -- surjectivity: every section of `𝓘 ^ n M` over `V` is a combination of restrictions
  have hle : chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowSubmodule I n M) V
      ≤ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (chartRestrictLinear M φ ''
          (chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowSubmodule I n M) U :
            Set (M.val.obj (op U)))) := by
    rw [chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine B S hS F hF I M hMcart hIcart n hU,
      chartSubmodule_idealPowSubmodule_eq_of_isAffine B S hS F hF I M hMcart hIcart n hV]
    exact pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_span_image B S hS F hF I M n φ
      (hMcart U V hU hV φ).2 (hIcart U V hU hV φ).2
  rw [chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top]
  refine top_unique fun y _ => ?_
  -- the sections of `𝓘 ^ n M` over `V` carried into `M(V)` along the inclusion
  set Z : Submodule (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (M.val.obj (op V)) :=
    Submodule.map ((idealPowModuleι I n M).val.app (op V)).hom
      (Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V)
        (Set.range fun x : (idealPowModule I n M).val.obj (op U) =>
          chartRestrictLinear (idealPowModule I n M) φ x)) with hZ
  have hsub : chartRestrictLinear M φ ''
      (chartSubmodule B S hS F hF (idealPowSubmodule I n M) U : Set (M.val.obj (op U)))
      ⊆ (Z : Set (M.val.obj (op V))) := by
    rintro z ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨chartRestrictLinear (idealPowModule I n M) φ ⟨x, hx⟩,
      Submodule.subset_span ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    exact PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (idealPowModuleι I n M).val φ.op ⟨x, hx⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwy⟩ : ((idealPowModuleι I n M).val.app (op V)).hom y ∈ Z :=
    Submodule.span_le.2 hsub (hle y.2)
  exact (Subtype.ext hwy : w = y) ▸ hw

/-- **`𝓘 ^ n M` is quasi-coherent** for `𝓘` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `M` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-module.

This is the statement whose absence the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentAdicSystem` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoherentAdicSystemProperSupport` record as the obstruction
to the completion functor of Stacks 08B4. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowSubmodule (I : IdealSheaves B S hS F hF)
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (hM : M.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hI : I.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (n : ℕ) :
    (idealPowModule I n M).IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
  isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts _
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF I M
      (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF M hM)
      (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF I.toSheafOfModules hI) n)

/-! ### The two spellings of `𝓘 ^ n M` agree -/

/-- **The two spellings of `𝓘 ^ n M` on an algebraic space agree**, with no hypothesis on `M` or
on `𝓘`: the local-membership closure `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule` of the chartwise
products and the least sheaf submodule `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple` dominating
them are the same sheaf submodule of `M`.

Both are characterized by the same chartwise universal property —
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple_le_iff` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule_le_iff` test a sheaf submodule against containment of
`𝓘(U) ^ n · M(U)` over every chart — so each is below the other.  In particular the Artin–Rees
development of Stacks 07UL, stated for the first spelling, applies to the subsheaves out of which
the category `Coh(F, 𝓘)` is built, which use the second. -/
theorem idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSubmodule
    (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O))).Submodule)
    (n : ℕ) (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF) :
    idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M = idealPowSubmodule 𝓘 n M := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [idealPowerMultiple_le_iff]
    intro U
    exact pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_le_chartSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 n U
  · rw [idealPowSubmodule_le_iff]
    intro X
    exact le_idealPowerMultiple_obj B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M X.unop

/-- **`𝓘 ^ n M` is quasi-coherent**, for the spelling
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple` out of which the category `Coh(F, 𝓘)` of coherent
`𝓘`-adic systems is built. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowerMultiple
    (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O))).Submodule)
    (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF) (hM : M.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hI : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (n : ℕ) :
    (idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M).toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  rw [idealPowerMultiple_eq_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M]
  exact isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowSubmodule B S hS F hF 𝓘 M hM hI n

/-! ### Coherence of `𝓘 ^ n M` and of `M / 𝓘 ^ n M` -/

/-- **`𝓘 ^ n M` is coherent** for coherent `M` on a locally Noetherian algebraic space: it is a
quasi-coherent submodule of `M`, so the submodule clause of Stacks 07UD applies. -/
theorem isCoherent_idealPowerMultiple
    [Fact (HasEtaleLocalProperty B S hS F (fun V : Scheme.{u} => IsLocallyNoetherian V))]
    (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O))).Submodule)
    (hI : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (hM : IsCoherent B S hS F hF M) (n : ℕ) :
    IsCoherent B S hS F hF (idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M).toSheafOfModules :=
  isCoherent_of_mono_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF
    (idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M).ι
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 M hM.toIsQuasicoherentOnSite hI n) hM

/-- **`M / 𝓘 ^ n M` is coherent** for coherent `M` on a locally Noetherian algebraic space.

This is the well-definedness of the terms of the completion of `M` along `𝓘`, and the statement
the completion functor of Stacks 08B4 is built on: the quotient is the cokernel of the inclusion
of `𝓘 ^ n M`, both of whose ends are now coherent, so the cokernel clause of Stacks 07UC
applies. -/
theorem isCoherent_idealPowerQuotient
    [Fact (HasEtaleLocalProperty B S hS F (fun V : Scheme.{u} => IsLocallyNoetherian V))]
    (𝓘 : (SheafOfModules.unit
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O))).Submodule)
    (hI : 𝓘.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (hM : IsCoherent B S hS F hF M) (n : ℕ) :
    IsCoherent B S hS F hF (idealPowerQuotient B S hS F hF 𝓘 n M) :=
  isCoherent_cokernel B S hS F hF
    (isCoherent_idealPowerMultiple B S hS F hF 𝓘 hI M hM n) hM _

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
